#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0522 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "ACTARMCD column absent while ACTARM is populated. THE ALL-FACET GATE, NEW WITH D-16 (owner ruling 2026-09-12, executed 2026-09-13): the Check's bare empty(ACTARMCD) leaf would fire once per ACTARM-populated row under absent = all-missing, exactly as the L1-equivalent FDA/PMDA-SD1362 did before OR-wave 1 pinned them. Requirements.Variables.All [ACTARMCD, ACTARM] now rejects the dataset, SKIPPED naming the variable - ruling in documentation/derivation/absent-column-verdicts.tsv (verdict 2-2). Row 1 WOULD fire were the gate removed. If this scenario EXECUTES, the gate has been removed: escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ACTARM   type=Char label="Description of Actual Arm"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | Treatment A
